message.content:
{"diagnosis": "Trace window is sparse showing only TRAP asserted with tohost FAIL 0xdead on 256-word NOP stream where no trap is expected and fetch progress is expected. CYCLES=2009 indicates the core ran to trap/timeout instead of clean progress. Root cause in excerpt line 1446 is decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done, which retriggers the decoder on mem_done and can mis-decode a NOP as illegal, raising the observed trap.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1442,8 +1442,8 @@
 		if (ENABLE_IRQ && ENABLE_IRQ_TIMER && timer) begin
 			timer <= timer - 1;
 		end
-		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done;
+		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst;
 		decoder_trigger_q <= decoder_trigger;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger <= 0;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger_q <= decoder_pseudo_trigger;
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP asserted, fetch progress completes through 256 NOPs"}

